WEBVTT

00:07.799 --> 00:10.885
[somber music playing]

00:13.805 --> 00:14.848
[Julian] Francis.

00:18.435 --> 00:21.146
It's painful, I know,
but try to remember.

00:23.940 --> 00:25.316
[ominous music]

00:25.316 --> 00:27.027
[Julian] Go back to that time.

00:27.152 --> 00:28.945
[rumbling]

00:28.945 --> 00:30.321
[Julian] Go back.

00:31.281 --> 00:32.657
[door buzzer buzzing]

00:33.491 --> 00:34.576
[somber music playing]

00:52.177 --> 00:54.346
[buzzing continues]

01:06.858 --> 01:10.528
[buzzing continues]

01:10.653 --> 01:11.696
[Rex] Fran, it's me.

01:15.700 --> 01:16.576
Fran?

01:17.369 --> 01:18.703
It's me.

01:20.330 --> 01:22.374
Come on, doll. Open up.

01:24.417 --> 01:27.962
- [clock ticking]
- [liquid pouring]

01:27.962 --> 01:29.005
[clattering]

01:29.005 --> 01:30.423
[Rex] You getting any sleep?

01:34.052 --> 01:36.054
[clock chiming]

01:43.103 --> 01:44.729
[liquid pouring]

01:48.483 --> 01:49.776
[Rex] They were good boys.

01:55.240 --> 01:57.409
It might do you some good
to get out of the house.

01:58.827 --> 02:00.286
I'm worried about you, Fran.

02:02.539 --> 02:04.833
And I wish you'd let me pay
for their funeral.

02:04.833 --> 02:06.751
Give Jack and Benny
a nice send-off.

02:07.919 --> 02:09.045
I could talk to Father Vincent.

02:09.045 --> 02:10.088
- I'm sure--
- Why?

02:10.714 --> 02:12.507
So people can shove tissues
in my face

02:12.507 --> 02:14.426
and tell me it was God's will?

02:15.301 --> 02:18.304
I don't need a public display
to mourn my boys.

02:20.974 --> 02:23.351
Oz has been coming around
the store a lot lately.

02:24.769 --> 02:28.606
Says you won't speak to him
and barely look him in the eye.

02:28.732 --> 02:32.610
Oswald has always been
so goddamn needy.

02:34.154 --> 02:36.114
I'd made peace with it. I did.

02:36.990 --> 02:38.366
That he was different.

02:40.243 --> 02:42.370
But now, what he's done,
I can't.

02:43.121 --> 02:43.955
[inhales shakily]

02:46.332 --> 02:47.709
What's he done?

02:52.839 --> 02:53.715
Fran?

02:55.133 --> 02:57.802
[clattering, thud]

03:02.098 --> 03:04.476
[sniffs] I found this
in his coat.

03:06.686 --> 03:07.687
I don't...

03:07.812 --> 03:09.064
He was with 'em, Rex.

03:10.607 --> 03:11.483
He lied to me.

03:12.275 --> 03:13.318
He came home,

03:14.110 --> 03:15.403
actin' all sad,

03:15.403 --> 03:16.654
like he was the victim,

03:16.654 --> 03:17.697
but he knew.

03:17.989 --> 03:19.949
My babies were drowning
in those tunnels,

03:19.949 --> 03:21.743
and he didn't say
a goddamn word.

03:23.453 --> 03:25.538
He had every chance,
every goddamn chance,

03:25.538 --> 03:27.040
to say somethin',
to do somethin',

03:27.165 --> 03:28.541
anything, to stop it.

03:28.541 --> 03:30.710
- He's a kid.
- He locked them inside.

03:32.379 --> 03:34.506
The room where they found them,
the cops told me,

03:34.631 --> 03:37.175
they had to pry the fuckin' door
open to reach 'em.

03:38.968 --> 03:41.179
[crying] If I had known,
if he had just...

03:41.304 --> 03:42.180
I coulda saved 'em.

03:42.305 --> 03:43.890
They'd be here with me
right now.

03:44.015 --> 03:46.101
[breathing shakily]

03:46.101 --> 03:48.603
But Oswald didn't want that.
No. This is what he wanted.

03:48.603 --> 03:51.189
Me. [sniffs] All to himself.

03:51.856 --> 03:53.108
[Francis swallows hard]

03:55.318 --> 03:57.445
I got the devil
in my house, Rex.

03:59.698 --> 04:01.408
What the hell
am I supposed to do?

04:11.042 --> 04:12.210
There are
a couple different ways

04:12.335 --> 04:13.920
to handle
this type of situation.

04:15.880 --> 04:17.924
If Oz is what you say,

04:18.842 --> 04:20.969
well, guys like him,

04:21.845 --> 04:23.471
they can serve a purpose,

04:24.097 --> 04:25.557
go on to do big fuckin' things,

04:25.682 --> 04:27.350
especially in my line of work.

04:27.350 --> 04:28.852
But you gotta know
how to control them.

04:29.894 --> 04:32.939
Mostly, guys that come to me say
they're lookin' to make money.

04:33.064 --> 04:34.149
Now, that's fine.

04:34.149 --> 04:36.818
But greed don't buy loyalty.

04:38.069 --> 04:39.404
I want loyalty,

04:40.739 --> 04:42.657
I bring in guys
who are lookin' for a father.

04:43.199 --> 04:45.535
Guys like that
got a void to fill.

04:45.535 --> 04:47.078
They'll do anything for me.

04:48.288 --> 04:51.249
Now, Oswald...

04:52.042 --> 04:53.251
he don't need a father.

04:55.587 --> 04:56.629
He's got you.

04:57.797 --> 04:58.673
[Francis] Hmm.

04:58.673 --> 05:00.133
He's devoted to you.

05:00.967 --> 05:02.260
You can use that.

05:03.261 --> 05:06.431
Foster what he's got,
embrace it, raise it.

05:08.767 --> 05:09.809
Maybe he'd be great.

05:11.811 --> 05:13.646
Or maybe not. I don't know.
[chuckles]

05:14.939 --> 05:16.483
You have to bet on him to see.

05:17.484 --> 05:19.110
You want me
to look the other way?

05:19.986 --> 05:21.363
Ignore what he's done?

05:23.740 --> 05:25.367
What kind of mother
would I be...

05:26.785 --> 05:27.869
if I...

05:30.747 --> 05:31.623
I can't.

05:39.422 --> 05:40.965
Well then, maybe let him go.

05:44.094 --> 05:46.346
By "let him go," you mean...

05:55.689 --> 05:56.815
[sniffs]

06:01.027 --> 06:03.363
You'd be willin' to help me
with somethin' like that?

06:06.157 --> 06:07.492
[suspenseful music playing]

06:13.373 --> 06:15.000
- [knock on door]
- [music ends]

06:15.125 --> 06:16.001
[young Oz] Ma?

06:16.918 --> 06:18.169
I got dinner for ya.

06:19.504 --> 06:21.089
[tray clinks on floor]

06:26.469 --> 06:27.512
You're up.

06:28.471 --> 06:29.723
Get dressed.

06:30.682 --> 06:31.516
We're goin' out.

06:33.727 --> 06:35.020
Go on. Your suit.

06:37.397 --> 06:41.276
♪ There may be trouble ahead ♪

06:43.778 --> 06:47.866
♪ But while there's moonlight
and music ♪

06:47.991 --> 06:53.288
♪ And love and romance ♪

06:53.288 --> 06:57.250
♪ Let's face the music
and dance ♪

06:59.836 --> 07:05.800
♪ Before the fiddlers
have fled ♪

07:05.800 --> 07:07.385
Ma, look who's here.

07:07.385 --> 07:11.097
♪ Before they ask us
to pay the bill... ♪

07:11.681 --> 07:12.891
Yeah, sweetheart.

07:14.601 --> 07:16.227
Rex is gonna
drive you home later.

07:16.353 --> 07:18.271
- Really?
- Really.

07:19.522 --> 07:21.191
I know I been absent lately,

07:21.191 --> 07:24.069
so I wanted to make tonight
extra special.

07:26.029 --> 07:27.322
I know you miss 'em, Ma.

07:29.908 --> 07:30.950
I do too.

07:33.912 --> 07:38.083
♪ And then ♪

07:38.083 --> 07:41.878
♪ There may be teardrops
to shed ♪

07:41.878 --> 07:43.797
- [song fades]
- [ominous music playing]

07:44.631 --> 07:45.757
[Francis] No, wait.

07:46.758 --> 07:48.301
[Julian] Everything's all right.

07:50.720 --> 07:52.222
- Francis.
- [Francis] Wait. What are you...

07:52.222 --> 07:54.265
Let's just try and stay
in the moment, okay?

07:54.391 --> 07:55.433
Huh?

07:55.975 --> 07:58.144
[Julian] You're with Oswald,
your son.

07:58.812 --> 07:59.771
[Francis] Hmm.

08:00.230 --> 08:02.107
[Julian] You took him
to the jazz club, Monroe's.

08:04.609 --> 08:05.652
Go with it.

08:07.153 --> 08:08.154
[mumbles]

08:08.780 --> 08:09.698
I did...

08:12.242 --> 08:13.284
That's right.

08:18.623 --> 08:20.333
- [young Oz] Ma?
- [jazz music resumes]

08:22.210 --> 08:23.086
[young Oz] Ma?

08:23.628 --> 08:25.505
I'm gonna take care of you, Ma.

08:27.173 --> 08:28.299
You know that, right?

08:29.718 --> 08:32.679
You've been workin' so hard
for the three of us.

08:33.722 --> 08:35.390
It's gonna be easier now.

08:35.390 --> 08:36.725
I'll get a job.

08:37.434 --> 08:38.727
And I got all kinds of ideas

08:38.727 --> 08:40.645
on how to make cash
on the side, too.

08:40.645 --> 08:42.188
Yeah, you sound like
your father.

08:42.772 --> 08:43.857
That ain't true.

08:45.608 --> 08:47.027
I mean what I say.

08:49.446 --> 08:50.655
What do you want?

08:51.948 --> 08:53.491
Tell me, and I'll get it.

08:53.491 --> 08:54.659
[Francis] What do I want?

08:54.784 --> 08:57.328
You got it all figured out,
don't you?

08:58.121 --> 08:59.622
Look at you.

08:59.622 --> 09:01.332
Your balls have barely dropped,

09:01.332 --> 09:03.043
and you're gonna take care
of me?

09:03.043 --> 09:04.836
Of course
I'm gonna take care of you.

09:07.130 --> 09:08.673
I'd do anything for you.

09:10.175 --> 09:11.217
I see you, Ma.

09:11.885 --> 09:13.345
In ways that other people don't.

09:14.137 --> 09:17.265
I see the way you smile
when you want people to think

09:17.265 --> 09:19.225
you're enjoying somethin'
you ain't.

09:20.435 --> 09:22.771
I see how you smoke more
when you're thinkin',

09:23.521 --> 09:25.190
and you drink more
when you're sad.

09:26.024 --> 09:27.692
I see how hard you work,

09:28.151 --> 09:29.402
how smart you are...

09:30.987 --> 09:33.531
and how you wish the people
who matter would notice...

09:34.699 --> 09:37.702
or the people like that
wouldn't matter at all.

09:38.995 --> 09:40.872
No one else believes in you
like me.

09:41.623 --> 09:44.542
No one else is gonna give you
what you deserve.

09:45.085 --> 09:47.045
I'm gonna get you
out of the Eastside, Ma.

09:47.796 --> 09:49.714
Put you up somewhere real nice.

09:50.382 --> 09:51.758
Better than what we got now.

09:51.883 --> 09:54.219
Yeah, better's easy
than where we are.

09:54.344 --> 09:55.679
The best then.

09:55.679 --> 09:58.014
On the top floor,
in a penthouse, like you want,

09:58.014 --> 10:00.725
with a view
of the whole friggin' city.

10:00.850 --> 10:04.020
I'll get you expensive clothes
and-and jewelry.

10:04.020 --> 10:05.438
Nice shit, too.

10:06.022 --> 10:08.316
The kind where people see you
on the street and think,

10:08.900 --> 10:10.068
"She's important."

10:10.694 --> 10:12.237
And if you don't believe me,

10:12.737 --> 10:14.114
well, you don't gotta.

10:14.948 --> 10:16.574
'Cause I'm gonna prove it to ya.

10:17.200 --> 10:18.576
Every damn day.

10:18.702 --> 10:20.370
[crowd applauding]

10:20.370 --> 10:21.496
Just...

10:23.081 --> 10:23.915
♪ Please tell me... ♪

10:23.915 --> 10:25.250
Just don't give up on me.

10:30.755 --> 10:35.969
♪ How much you care... ♪

10:36.094 --> 10:37.220
Come on, Ma.

10:37.220 --> 10:38.596
♪ Before we say ♪

10:38.722 --> 10:39.764
Dance with me.

10:39.889 --> 10:42.767
[ominous music playing]

10:42.767 --> 10:45.770
♪ Goodnight, my dear ♪

10:48.440 --> 10:51.609
[suspenseful music playing]

10:54.112 --> 10:55.739
[Victor] Left here. Left here.

10:55.739 --> 10:57.699
[tires screech]

11:01.286 --> 11:03.121
Come on. Come on.
Come on. Come on.

11:11.463 --> 11:12.630
[Link] What is that?

11:14.799 --> 11:16.217
[tires screech]

11:17.302 --> 11:20.013
- [sirens wailing]
- [people clamoring]

11:27.562 --> 11:28.855
[Victor] Oh, my God.

11:32.817 --> 11:34.986
Fuck. Oz.

11:36.780 --> 11:38.782
Hey, he could be hurt.
We gotta get down there.

11:38.782 --> 11:41.076
- Oz is probably dead.
- Gonna be crawling with cops.

11:41.076 --> 11:43.828
You don't know that, all right?
We gotta check. Let's go.

11:44.371 --> 11:46.164
Your friend has put us
in a dangerous position.

11:46.289 --> 11:47.415
[speaks Mandarin]

11:47.665 --> 11:49.918
- [man] Let's get outta here.
- Wait. Wait. That's it?

11:50.794 --> 11:52.712
We're here for the product,
not the Penguin.

11:53.338 --> 11:54.339
[tuts]

11:55.840 --> 11:57.300
Wow. You're all a bunch

11:57.300 --> 11:59.010
of fucking cowards,
you know that?

12:00.303 --> 12:01.179
What did you say?

12:02.263 --> 12:03.765
What the hell
do you even stand for?

12:03.765 --> 12:06.226
What, are you gonna let
the Maronis and Gigantes do

12:06.351 --> 12:07.936
whatever they fuckin' want?

12:07.936 --> 12:09.145
[dramatic music playing]

12:09.145 --> 12:10.355
This is my neighborhood!

12:10.814 --> 12:12.190
Look at it!

12:14.567 --> 12:18.780
The whole world, they treat us
like-like we don't matter,

12:18.780 --> 12:21.282
like we're fuckin' nothin'.
Are you just gonna run away now?

12:21.282 --> 12:22.742
That's bullshit! [grunts]

12:22.742 --> 12:24.536
Watch what you say.

12:24.536 --> 12:27.455
You gotta know your place,
or you're gonna catch a bullet.

12:28.206 --> 12:29.582
Then you really don't matter.

12:29.582 --> 12:30.709
[man] Let's go.

12:31.876 --> 12:33.920
[car doors opening]

12:34.045 --> 12:36.047
[panting]

12:39.009 --> 12:40.552
- [whimpering]
- [car doors closing]

12:40.677 --> 12:43.513
[engines starting]

12:43.513 --> 12:45.890
[people clamoring]

12:46.016 --> 12:48.226
[police officer] I need you
to step back.

12:48.351 --> 12:51.730
[crowd shouting indistinctly]

12:55.025 --> 12:58.319
[woman screaming]

13:00.697 --> 13:02.115
[police officer] Stand back!
Move it!

13:02.115 --> 13:04.951
- Go back to your homes!
- [man] What homes?

13:05.076 --> 13:07.037
[police officer 2] Stand back!
It's not safe!

13:07.037 --> 13:09.497
[dramatic music continues]

13:10.874 --> 13:12.125
[police officer]
Can't go in there.

13:12.125 --> 13:13.084
[Zeke] Victor!

13:15.211 --> 13:16.129
Victor!

13:17.130 --> 13:18.214
Zeke.

13:18.214 --> 13:20.091
Hey, man, what happened?
Where's Oz?

13:20.216 --> 13:22.427
Sofia... [breathing raggedly]
She blew it all up.

13:22.552 --> 13:24.763
What about Oz? Did he get out?

13:26.598 --> 13:27.766
[music fades out]

13:30.018 --> 13:32.520
- [scraping]
- [tape peeling]

13:34.397 --> 13:35.523
[click]

13:36.524 --> 13:38.651
[tape peeling]

13:38.777 --> 13:41.488
- [scraping]
- [tape peeling]

13:41.613 --> 13:42.864
[muffled grunting]

13:42.864 --> 13:44.366
[Julian] It's time to wake up.

13:47.035 --> 13:48.620
- [click]
- [muffled grunt]

13:48.745 --> 13:50.038
[Julian sighs]

13:54.501 --> 13:55.919
[muffled grunting]

13:55.919 --> 13:57.087
[thud]

13:57.087 --> 13:58.171
[grunts]

13:58.922 --> 14:00.674
- Oz?
- [muffled grunting]

14:02.467 --> 14:03.468
It's been a minute.

14:04.302 --> 14:05.637
[muffled grunting]

14:06.429 --> 14:08.973
[muffled screaming]

14:09.808 --> 14:12.644
[muffled screaming]

14:13.269 --> 14:18.692
[muffled screaming]

14:18.817 --> 14:20.902
[muffled groaning]

14:20.902 --> 14:22.654
[Francis grunting]

14:24.864 --> 14:26.908
You know,
when Berto and I were kids,

14:28.535 --> 14:30.704
we found this nest
out by the greenhouse

14:30.829 --> 14:32.622
with two baby birds inside.

14:32.622 --> 14:35.083
[muffled shouting]

14:35.083 --> 14:39.337
One of the birds
was bigger than the other one...

14:40.422 --> 14:41.423
stronger.

14:42.632 --> 14:45.760
And the mama bird
gave it more food.

14:45.760 --> 14:47.303
[muffled shouting]

14:47.303 --> 14:48.972
And I got nervous
for the smaller bird.

14:49.097 --> 14:50.140
[muffled shouting]

14:50.140 --> 14:54.102
It was so weak and frail,
you know?

14:54.102 --> 14:55.186
[muffled shouting]

14:55.311 --> 14:57.439
I... I thought
it was going to die.

14:57.439 --> 14:58.773
But then one morning,

14:59.524 --> 15:01.609
when the mama bird was away,

15:03.528 --> 15:04.738
the smaller bird...

15:06.364 --> 15:09.617
viciously attacked
the bigger bird...

15:10.702 --> 15:11.578
[tense music playing]

15:11.703 --> 15:12.704
...and killed it.

15:13.705 --> 15:16.124
And then it just pushed
its brother out of the nest.

15:19.836 --> 15:23.590
It was the most disturbing thing
I had ever seen.

15:24.341 --> 15:26.885
At least... at the time.

15:28.261 --> 15:29.679
Can you imagine?

15:29.679 --> 15:32.724
Doing something so terrible
to your own brother?

15:34.517 --> 15:36.227
But that's not even
the wildest part.

15:36.895 --> 15:38.438
When the mama bird came back

15:39.689 --> 15:43.401
and saw that one of her babies
was missing,

15:45.195 --> 15:46.571
guess what she did.

15:51.034 --> 15:52.077
Nothing.

15:54.204 --> 15:57.290
Instead of punishing
the smaller bird,

15:58.083 --> 16:02.420
she kept feeding it,
caring for it

16:02.545 --> 16:04.381
as if nothing even happened.

16:04.381 --> 16:05.590
[Francis exhales shakily]

16:06.424 --> 16:08.134
[Sofia] Do you think
the mother knew, Oz...

16:08.134 --> 16:09.594
[Francis groans]

16:09.719 --> 16:11.096
[Sofia] ...what her baby did?

16:13.139 --> 16:15.517
- Francis, what do you think?
- [Francis grunts]

16:15.517 --> 16:19.646
[muffled shouting]

16:19.771 --> 16:20.897
Should we find out?

16:20.897 --> 16:23.108
[muffled shouting]

16:23.233 --> 16:24.150
Whaddya say?

16:25.235 --> 16:26.986
Share some hard truths?

16:26.986 --> 16:28.655
It might bring about
some healing.

16:28.780 --> 16:30.365
- [muffled grunt]
- Oz?

16:30.365 --> 16:31.574
[muffled grunting]

16:32.450 --> 16:33.993
- Would you like to start?
- [Oz grunts]

16:33.993 --> 16:35.954
You fuckin' psycho!

16:36.079 --> 16:37.288
What is this shit?

16:37.414 --> 16:38.873
Talkin' about birds!

16:38.873 --> 16:40.458
Jesus Christ!

16:40.458 --> 16:41.459
You don't like my story?

16:41.584 --> 16:43.128
Ma! Ma, look at me!

16:43.253 --> 16:45.255
I'm gonna get you outta here.
I swear to God, Ma.

16:45.255 --> 16:46.923
I swear to God
I'm gonna get you outta here.

16:46.923 --> 16:48.800
- Oz... you're right.
- Ma!

16:49.634 --> 16:50.969
It was a stupid story.

16:52.721 --> 16:54.472
And you have
the better one anyway.

16:55.640 --> 16:56.516
So...

16:58.143 --> 16:59.436
tell us what happened.

16:59.436 --> 17:01.146
What are you talkin'...
What happened when?

17:01.688 --> 17:05.358
Tell us why
you left your brothers to die

17:05.483 --> 17:06.484
in those tunnels.

17:10.864 --> 17:12.240
What the hell
are you talkin' about?

17:12.240 --> 17:15.994
Why did you tell your mom
you weren't with them?

17:16.119 --> 17:17.454
Why did you lie to her?

17:17.454 --> 17:19.289
What the hell
are you talkin' about?!

17:19.289 --> 17:20.290
[Sofia] Stop pretending.

17:20.957 --> 17:22.917
She knows. I know.

17:23.460 --> 17:25.670
We all know what you did.

17:27.464 --> 17:28.757
You done somethin' to her.

17:30.300 --> 17:31.509
What the fuck
did you do to her?!

17:31.634 --> 17:34.054
You act like
you tell her everything.

17:34.846 --> 17:37.807
And she acts like
she believes you. Why?

17:37.807 --> 17:39.309
[grunts]

17:39.309 --> 17:42.771
Why are you both so afraid
of the truth?

17:42.771 --> 17:45.148
- Ma!
- [Sofia] It's so sick.

17:45.148 --> 17:46.107
[Oz] Ma!

17:47.359 --> 17:49.027
It's almost as sick

17:49.527 --> 17:54.574
as you asking that man
to kill your son.

17:55.867 --> 17:57.243
[breathing shakily]

17:57.243 --> 18:01.081
Rex, right? Was that his name?

18:01.831 --> 18:03.792
What kind of weird fuckin' games
are you tryin' to play?

18:04.417 --> 18:07.212
[feebly] Shut up. Shut up.
Just shut up.

18:07.337 --> 18:11.049
Your last night together
was going to be here,

18:11.174 --> 18:12.217
at this club.

18:13.051 --> 18:15.887
Right, Francis? Am I right?

18:16.012 --> 18:18.556
Was it over there?
Where you two danced?

18:18.682 --> 18:20.517
Is that where Oz made you
his promise?

18:20.517 --> 18:22.644
God damn it, stop.

18:22.644 --> 18:24.062
I just wanna know.

18:25.355 --> 18:27.273
- Was it worth it?
- [Francis] Fuck you.

18:27.273 --> 18:28.983
Did he give you
everything that you wanted?

18:28.983 --> 18:31.986
- Did he fulfill his promise?
- Fuck you. Fuck you.

18:31.986 --> 18:32.946
[Oz] Ma.

18:34.197 --> 18:35.115
Ma.

18:35.240 --> 18:36.783
Or do you wish
you would've let Rex

18:36.908 --> 18:38.576
take him for that ride?

18:41.287 --> 18:44.165
What did you lose
by keeping him alive?

18:45.583 --> 18:46.793
I know what I lost...

18:47.627 --> 18:49.004
what he took from me.

18:49.796 --> 18:53.258
He deserves to know
what he did to you,

18:54.092 --> 18:55.969
how you feel about him,

18:56.094 --> 18:59.347
and how... how angry you are.

19:01.766 --> 19:02.600
Tell him.

19:04.310 --> 19:05.270
Tell him.

19:08.982 --> 19:10.191
Yeah.

19:15.822 --> 19:17.490
[menacing music playing]

19:24.372 --> 19:25.248
Fine.

19:26.916 --> 19:27.792
Julian.

19:29.961 --> 19:30.962
[Oz] What the fuck?

19:32.464 --> 19:33.298
What are you doin'?

19:33.965 --> 19:35.008
Stay away from her!

19:36.426 --> 19:38.720
Ma! Don't fuckin' touch her!

19:38.720 --> 19:41.681
Don't you fuckin' touch her!
Don't fuckin' touch her!

19:41.806 --> 19:44.476
- [Francis] No! No!
- Oz, was it my brother's right

19:44.601 --> 19:46.811
or left pinky
that you chopped off?

19:46.936 --> 19:48.730
Jesus, no, Sofia!

19:48.730 --> 19:51.483
- It was the right.
- Hey! Don't fuckin' touch her!

19:51.608 --> 19:53.735
- Oswald!
- [Oz] Don't fuckin' do it!

19:53.735 --> 19:56.946
- [Francis screaming]
- [Oz screams]

19:56.946 --> 19:58.865
Oz! [screaming]

19:58.990 --> 19:59.991
No! Jesus!

20:00.116 --> 20:01.201
[Sofia] Here's the thing.

20:01.701 --> 20:04.162
Just because
somebody knows something,

20:04.287 --> 20:06.164
doesn't mean that
they don't need to hear it

20:06.289 --> 20:08.833
- from the person who hurt them.
- Don't. Sofia, don't.

20:08.958 --> 20:12.128
I will never get that
from my father.

20:12.128 --> 20:15.131
But I'm offering you
the opportunity

20:15.131 --> 20:16.299
to give it to your mother.

20:16.299 --> 20:17.717
[Francis screaming] No!

20:17.842 --> 20:19.219
She deserves the best.

20:19.219 --> 20:20.720
- [screaming]
- [Sofia] Doesn't she?

20:20.845 --> 20:23.306
- [Francis] No! No!
- Oz, doesn't she?

20:23.306 --> 20:25.475
- So give her your best.
- Sofia, don't fuckin' do it!

20:25.475 --> 20:26.851
Just don't do it!
She did nothin'.

20:26.976 --> 20:27.852
It's very simple.

20:28.061 --> 20:30.188
All you have to do
is tell the truth.

20:30.647 --> 20:32.524
Tell her what you did
to your brothers,

20:32.649 --> 20:34.150
and tell her why,

20:34.150 --> 20:35.652
and then we can all
take a breath.

20:35.652 --> 20:38.071
This is fuckin' insane!

20:38.071 --> 20:39.364
[Francis wails]

20:39.489 --> 20:41.658
I already told ya,
I didn't do fuckin' shit.

20:41.658 --> 20:43.618
I don't know what
you're fuckin' talkin' about.

20:43.618 --> 20:44.953
[Francis shrieking] Oz!

20:44.953 --> 20:46.496
[Oz] Don't! God damn it, don't!

20:46.496 --> 20:48.289
I did nothin'!
I wasn't even there!

20:48.289 --> 20:49.833
- She knows that. Stop!
- Admit it.

20:49.833 --> 20:51.710
I wasn't even with 'em.
I didn't do shit.

20:51.710 --> 20:53.753
- What is wrong with you?
- She knows. Ma!

20:53.878 --> 20:55.213
Just tell her for her sake.

20:55.338 --> 20:56.589
Tell her I was with you.

20:56.589 --> 20:58.258
It's my fuckin' finger,
you spineless prick!

20:58.383 --> 20:59.676
I was with you.

20:59.676 --> 21:02.095
Jesus, just say it. Tell her.

21:02.220 --> 21:04.097
I already fuckin' know.

21:04.222 --> 21:05.265
[music ends abruptly]

21:09.060 --> 21:10.645
[breathing heavily]

21:12.230 --> 21:14.816
I know what you did
to Jack and Benny.

21:14.816 --> 21:16.776
I always known.

21:22.073 --> 21:23.116
Lies.

21:25.368 --> 21:26.870
You're gettin' things confused.

21:29.122 --> 21:30.915
It's just your disease talkin',
Ma.

21:31.041 --> 21:32.083
Fuck you!

21:33.626 --> 21:35.712
I hate you. I hate you
for what you did.

21:35.712 --> 21:37.297
I never stopped hating you.

21:38.256 --> 21:39.924
[Francis breathing heavily]

21:40.467 --> 21:41.509
[Sofia] That's enough.

21:43.261 --> 21:44.346
[Francis pants]

21:45.472 --> 21:46.806
[gasping]

21:50.101 --> 21:52.979
You woulda let me cut it off, huh?

21:55.273 --> 21:56.775
You woulda let me do it.

21:58.860 --> 22:00.362
Because you don't care
about her.

22:00.362 --> 22:01.780
- Fuck you.
- You don't.

22:02.655 --> 22:03.698
Not enough.

22:04.908 --> 22:06.159
Not like you say.

22:08.787 --> 22:10.663
You don't feel a fuckin' thing.

22:12.916 --> 22:14.125
[Francis, feebly] Oswald.

22:16.127 --> 22:18.797
I had enough to give, Oswald.

22:20.757 --> 22:22.967
I had enough to give
all three of you.

22:24.928 --> 22:26.513
You didn't have to leave 'em
down there.

22:26.513 --> 22:28.473
You didn't have
to take 'em from me.

22:30.517 --> 22:32.227
They were my babies.

22:32.936 --> 22:34.145
My world.

22:35.563 --> 22:36.981
Your brothers.

22:50.120 --> 22:51.830
You're a disappointment.

22:53.331 --> 22:54.874
You're a waste of space.

22:56.334 --> 22:59.212
I wake up every goddamn day
sick that I'm your mother.

23:00.005 --> 23:01.381
[sniffs] She's right.

23:02.340 --> 23:03.717
She's fuckin' right.

23:05.510 --> 23:08.388
I shoulda let Rex kill ya
when I had the chance.

23:10.390 --> 23:11.349
[glass shatters]

23:11.349 --> 23:12.517
[Francis shouts]

23:13.309 --> 23:16.396
[Oz grunting]

23:17.397 --> 23:18.314
You're the devil.

23:18.314 --> 23:19.691
[Oz gasping]

23:19.816 --> 23:21.234
You're the goddamn devil.

23:22.485 --> 23:25.697
[Oz gasps, grunts]

23:26.364 --> 23:27.198
[grunts]

23:27.991 --> 23:28.908
[shakily] Ma.

23:29.826 --> 23:30.827
[gasps]

23:30.827 --> 23:34.497
- [rain pouring]
- [thunder rumbling]

23:34.497 --> 23:37.917
♪ There may be teardrops
to shed ♪

23:37.917 --> 23:39.127
[glass shatters]

23:39.878 --> 23:40.962
Jack?

23:40.962 --> 23:42.797
♪ So while there's moonlight ♪

23:42.797 --> 23:44.466
[Oz grunting]

23:44.466 --> 23:45.550
Benny.

23:45.550 --> 23:49.220
♪ And love and romance... ♪

23:49.346 --> 23:50.555
My babies.

23:50.680 --> 23:53.266
[water dripping]

23:53.892 --> 23:55.310
I'm sorry.

23:55.310 --> 23:56.436
[Oz] Ma.

23:59.105 --> 24:01.316
[mutters] I'm sor--

24:03.234 --> 24:04.736
[Francis mutters]

24:06.029 --> 24:07.155
I'm...

24:10.742 --> 24:11.785
Ma!

24:12.952 --> 24:13.995
- Ma!
- [snapping]

24:14.621 --> 24:15.455
[Sofia] Stop him!

24:15.580 --> 24:16.664
[dramatic music playing]

24:18.917 --> 24:21.753
[gunfire]

24:21.878 --> 24:23.421
- [shouts]
- [gunfire]

24:23.546 --> 24:25.215
- [bullet ricochets]
- Ma!

24:25.215 --> 24:26.841
[gunfire]

24:26.841 --> 24:28.885
Come on. I got you. I got you.

24:28.885 --> 24:33.598
[gunfire]

24:34.391 --> 24:35.934
[upbeat song playing]

24:35.934 --> 24:38.645
♪ My love, I'm sending... ♪

24:38.645 --> 24:40.397
Ah!

24:40.397 --> 24:41.314
[gunshot]

24:41.439 --> 24:43.817
[menacing music playing]

24:48.071 --> 24:49.322
[Oz grunts]

24:50.156 --> 24:51.282
You're gonna be all right.

24:53.785 --> 24:54.953
[tires screech]

24:56.788 --> 24:58.164
[gunshot]

24:58.164 --> 25:00.500
- [tires screech]
- [horn honks]

25:07.007 --> 25:08.591
She just fell.
She just hit her head.

25:08.591 --> 25:09.884
She's not making sense.

25:09.884 --> 25:11.970
She's got this condition,
Lewy body,

25:12.095 --> 25:13.304
dementia-type thing.

25:13.430 --> 25:15.181
Ma, you're gonna be
all right. You hear me?

25:15.181 --> 25:16.766
Stay in the waiting room.
We'll find you.

25:16.766 --> 25:18.143
Gonna be able to fix her, right?

25:18.268 --> 25:20.145
We'll do everything we can, sir.

25:20.270 --> 25:21.563
Just stay nearby.

25:22.605 --> 25:26.568
[indistinct announcement
over PA]

25:26.568 --> 25:28.111
[newscaster]
GC1 is live at the scene

25:28.111 --> 25:29.571
of chaos in downtown Gotham.

25:29.571 --> 25:31.489
Rescue workers pull bodies
from the rubble

25:31.614 --> 25:34.075
as authorities continue
to search for the cause

25:34.075 --> 25:36.327
of a deadly explosion
in Crown Point.

25:36.453 --> 25:37.662
[newscast continues
indistinctly]

25:37.787 --> 25:39.330
[Oz winces]

25:40.290 --> 25:41.499
[ominous music playing]

25:44.461 --> 25:46.546
[Oz grunts]

25:46.546 --> 25:49.549
[Victor] Oz, it's me again.
I'm worried, all right?

25:49.549 --> 25:51.843
Just call me back.
Please call me back.

25:51.968 --> 25:55.221
- [sighs]
- [phone vibrating]

25:59.476 --> 26:00.935
[Oz] Kid, where the hell are ya?

26:00.935 --> 26:01.895
Oz!

26:02.520 --> 26:03.688
[groans]

26:04.856 --> 26:05.982
[grunts]

26:05.982 --> 26:08.068
Fuck. [sighs]

26:08.068 --> 26:09.194
[breathing shakily]

26:09.903 --> 26:12.280
[grunting]

26:18.912 --> 26:21.373
- [stapler clicks]
- [grunts]

26:24.334 --> 26:25.585
- [grunts]
- [stapler clicks]

26:27.379 --> 26:28.463
[Victor] Oz?

26:28.672 --> 26:30.548
- In here. Shut the door, kid.
- [door closes]

26:30.674 --> 26:32.676
- Holy shit!
- [stapler clicks]

26:32.676 --> 26:34.636
What happened? Are you okay?

26:35.553 --> 26:36.471
Yeah.

26:36.471 --> 26:38.973
Sofia, you know, she stabbed me.

26:38.973 --> 26:40.517
She fucked with my ma too.

26:40.517 --> 26:43.395
Wh-wh-what did she do to her?

26:44.771 --> 26:47.732
Just, uh, pass me
one of those, um...

26:47.857 --> 26:49.776
yeah, patch, bandage thing.

26:49.901 --> 26:53.363
[grunts, pants] Fuck.

26:53.363 --> 26:55.281
[wincing]

26:55.281 --> 26:56.408
[plastic rustling]

26:58.076 --> 27:01.246
- [Oz grunting]
- Your mom, is she all right?

27:01.955 --> 27:02.997
Yeah, she will be.

27:04.040 --> 27:06.376
- [grunts]
- [Victor] I'm sorry, Oz.

27:06.376 --> 27:09.129
I-I-I got there too late.

27:09.754 --> 27:12.298
I tried the gangs. I tried to...

27:13.049 --> 27:14.426
m-m-make 'em see,

27:14.551 --> 27:16.428
but they... they just left.

27:16.553 --> 27:17.637
It ain't you, Vic.

27:18.388 --> 27:19.264
It ain't you.

27:19.931 --> 27:21.057
Just the way it is.

27:21.641 --> 27:23.101
I got nothin' left
to offer 'em, so...

27:23.643 --> 27:24.769
That's not true.

27:25.645 --> 27:26.771
No. You're wrong.

27:27.230 --> 27:30.775
Oz, it's not just
about the... th-the drugs

27:31.401 --> 27:32.694
or-or the money.

27:32.694 --> 27:35.196
I mean, that's...
that's part of it, sure, but...

27:37.907 --> 27:39.117
I mean, guys like Link,

27:40.535 --> 27:42.162
h-he believes in you.

27:42.287 --> 27:43.329
- Link?
- Yes.

27:43.455 --> 27:44.539
[Oz laughs]

27:44.539 --> 27:46.458
Link's a fuckin' deputy, kid.

27:47.459 --> 27:48.710
Can't do shit
without the Dai Lo.

27:48.710 --> 27:51.212
God damn it, Oz, listen to me!

27:53.882 --> 27:56.134
You gave people jobs
in Crown Point.

27:58.219 --> 27:59.763
You got the power back on.

27:59.763 --> 28:01.056
Yeah.

28:02.307 --> 28:03.516
Nobody did that.

28:04.601 --> 28:06.978
All right? Nobody else did that.
Nobody even tried.

28:10.315 --> 28:11.900
You gave people dignity.
[beats chest]

28:14.778 --> 28:17.989
Bliss? That's bigger than Bliss.
All right? So...

28:19.366 --> 28:20.283
[claps hands]

28:20.283 --> 28:22.035
G-get the hell up. Let's go.

28:22.160 --> 28:24.329
Get your shit together
and, uh...

28:25.997 --> 28:27.082
you know...

28:29.000 --> 28:29.876
be you.

28:31.670 --> 28:32.671
[breathing heavily]

28:32.796 --> 28:34.172
Y-you, uh...

28:36.341 --> 28:37.258
You practiced that, huh?

28:37.967 --> 28:38.760
Shut up.

28:38.760 --> 28:41.054
No, no, it's good. It's good.

28:41.179 --> 28:43.640
You gotta project more,
you know, from your gut.

28:43.640 --> 28:45.016
[chuckles]

28:45.975 --> 28:48.603
All right, let's get the fuck
outta here. Help me up.

28:49.688 --> 28:51.147
- [Oz grunts]
- All right.

28:51.731 --> 28:54.025
[grunts] Sofia's gonna be
expectin' a brawl.

28:54.859 --> 28:56.569
So we're gonna come
at her sideways, all right?

28:56.569 --> 28:57.904
What about your mom?

28:58.488 --> 29:02.033
[spluttering] She'll never look
at me again, all right?

29:02.826 --> 29:04.035
Unless I get this done.

29:06.204 --> 29:07.372
Got a promise to keep.

29:08.581 --> 29:09.874
[indistinct chatter]

29:11.209 --> 29:12.502
[crowd falls silent]

29:12.502 --> 29:15.463
Thank you for making the trip
across the bridge.

29:15.463 --> 29:17.549
- I know it's a hike.
- [bottle thuds]

29:18.508 --> 29:21.970
This was my father's home.
And as you can imagine,

29:21.970 --> 29:26.307
a lot of... terrible shit
happened here.

29:26.850 --> 29:28.268
- Now...
- [bottle thuds]

29:28.393 --> 29:30.437
What I wanna know is...

29:30.562 --> 29:32.230
[munching]

29:32.230 --> 29:33.565
Who wants it?

29:35.358 --> 29:38.445
[Sofia swishes liquid, swallows]

29:39.029 --> 29:41.614
I don't think we're quite clear
on what you're offering.

29:46.536 --> 29:47.871
I'm leaving Gotham,

29:48.413 --> 29:49.664
Mr. Zhao.

29:50.999 --> 29:52.625
There's nothing left
for me here.

29:54.461 --> 29:55.337
But my home,

29:56.421 --> 29:57.464
my territories,

29:58.214 --> 29:59.299
my businesses...

30:01.092 --> 30:02.135
can all be yours.

30:03.261 --> 30:04.929
Well, not all of yours.

30:06.056 --> 30:08.266
Whichever one of you
brings me Oz first.

30:08.391 --> 30:09.684
[chuckling]

30:09.684 --> 30:10.935
He's dead.

30:12.270 --> 30:13.355
He's not.

30:14.981 --> 30:16.900
I'm gonna make this very simple.

30:17.442 --> 30:20.445
Whoever finds Oz first

30:21.112 --> 30:24.324
can have all the means
to control Gotham...

30:24.949 --> 30:27.035
for as long
as they can hold onto it.

30:27.786 --> 30:28.870
This isn't real.

30:29.496 --> 30:30.538
[dramatic music playing]

30:30.538 --> 30:31.664
Right?

30:32.415 --> 30:34.793
You want us to believe
you're gonna walk away from...

30:35.460 --> 30:36.461
all of this?

30:38.421 --> 30:39.381
Why would you do that?

30:41.299 --> 30:42.467
Because I can.

30:44.844 --> 30:45.887
[glass thuds on table]

30:48.181 --> 30:49.849
[tuts] So, who wants it?

30:51.935 --> 30:53.770
All right, you stay put.
Don't do anything

30:53.770 --> 30:55.980
that might call attention
to yourself, all right?

30:56.648 --> 30:58.566
We may have to get out of here
real quick.

30:58.566 --> 31:00.485
- Yeah.
- Here, put the gun in the glove.

31:12.163 --> 31:13.832
[Oz grunts]

31:14.874 --> 31:16.876
All right, how do I look?

31:20.880 --> 31:21.715
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

31:21.840 --> 31:23.258
Yeah, you look... It's good.

31:23.258 --> 31:25.301
- No blood, so...
- Yeah, good.

31:25.301 --> 31:27.512
Lookin' the part's
only half the thing, you know.

31:27.637 --> 31:28.847
- [Victor] Mmm.
- All right.

31:29.973 --> 31:31.599
Into the fuckin' lion's den.

31:33.309 --> 31:34.769
[Oz breathing heavily]

31:34.769 --> 31:36.563
[phone vibrating]

31:48.867 --> 31:50.368
- Link?
- Victor.

31:51.369 --> 31:52.537
You with Oz?

31:54.039 --> 31:55.081
[Victor] Um...

31:57.167 --> 31:58.460
[Link] I know he's alive.

31:59.085 --> 32:00.587
Sofia just put a bounty
on his head.

32:01.713 --> 32:03.548
Listen, you were right.

32:04.090 --> 32:05.133
We gotta do something.

32:05.633 --> 32:06.926
But we gotta do it fast.

32:07.761 --> 32:09.721
Come on. Tell me where you at.

32:11.556 --> 32:12.474
[door opens]

32:16.519 --> 32:17.562
[door thuds shut]

32:19.272 --> 32:21.775
[footsteps echoing]

32:54.099 --> 32:55.266
Jesus Christ.

32:56.643 --> 32:58.978
What the fuck, Oswald?

32:59.604 --> 33:00.814
I did what you asked.

33:00.814 --> 33:02.440
If anybody sees me
in here with you, I'm--

33:02.565 --> 33:03.775
[gavel bangs loudly]

33:04.317 --> 33:05.318
[chuckles] Fuck.

33:06.027 --> 33:06.945
It works.

33:09.239 --> 33:10.281
You, uh...

33:11.241 --> 33:13.034
come a little closer,
Councilman?

33:14.452 --> 33:15.912
Nice acoustics in here,

33:15.912 --> 33:18.873
but, you know,
I prefer not to shout.

33:20.333 --> 33:21.626
Come on. I don't bite.

33:22.252 --> 33:23.211
There you go.

33:24.337 --> 33:26.756
Listen, I never got the chance
to thank you for helping me out.

33:26.756 --> 33:28.883
Crown Point's prettier
with lights.

33:28.883 --> 33:30.427
But they're, uh...

33:30.427 --> 33:32.887
They're pullin' bodies out
of the rubble down there now.

33:32.887 --> 33:34.305
It's fuckin' tragic.

33:35.473 --> 33:37.600
People are pointin' fingers,
you know.

33:37.600 --> 33:39.060
I mean, I guess
most of the fingers

33:39.060 --> 33:41.021
are gonna be pointed
at City Hall.

33:41.021 --> 33:43.898
"Fuck the man."
You know, that kinda shit.

33:43.898 --> 33:45.567
And if the voters want answers,

33:46.568 --> 33:48.153
sure would be nice
to have some, right?

33:48.695 --> 33:50.321
- Answers?
- Yeah.

33:50.864 --> 33:52.115
Like what kind of answers?

33:52.115 --> 33:53.658
Answers like the truth.

33:55.577 --> 33:57.871
Sofia Falcone, she sent
a car full of explosives

33:57.996 --> 33:59.622
into the tunnels under the city.

33:59.622 --> 34:00.582
[Hady] Mm-hmm.

34:00.582 --> 34:02.083
The damn thing went boom.

34:03.335 --> 34:04.836
And why would she do that?

34:07.505 --> 34:08.673
Because...

34:10.633 --> 34:12.010
that hole in the ground
used to be

34:12.135 --> 34:13.845
the biggest drug lab in Gotham.

34:15.347 --> 34:17.849
Run by a real smart
motherfucker, too.

34:21.394 --> 34:22.771
Salvatore Maroni.

34:23.938 --> 34:26.566
He's pushin' a new street drug
called Bliss.

34:26.691 --> 34:29.361
And you know all this how?

34:30.236 --> 34:32.489
Listen, I try to stay out
of these kinds of things,

34:32.489 --> 34:34.449
all right? But the headline is:

34:34.449 --> 34:35.909
it's the same old war.

34:36.034 --> 34:37.744
The Maronis and Falcones
rippin' each other off.

34:37.869 --> 34:39.871
The Maronis kill
Sofia's brother.

34:40.413 --> 34:41.706
She goes full psycho.

34:42.415 --> 34:44.751
She burns Sal's wife and son
to a crisp,

34:44.876 --> 34:46.544
blows up
his entire fuckin' operation.

34:46.670 --> 34:48.630
I mean, what a girl!
I gotta give her some credit.

34:48.630 --> 34:50.715
- That's quite a story.
- Yeah.

34:51.174 --> 34:53.134
Is any of it true?

34:54.302 --> 34:55.804
Yeah, it's fuckin' true.

34:55.804 --> 34:57.138
When the cops dig
in that hole,

34:57.138 --> 34:58.515
you know what
they're gonna find?

34:58.515 --> 35:00.725
They're gonna find little pieces
of Sofia's G-Wagen

35:01.226 --> 35:03.853
and a bunch of dead Falcones
and Maronis...

35:03.853 --> 35:05.647
including Salvatore himself.

35:07.315 --> 35:10.068
It is what it looks like.

35:11.403 --> 35:12.278
You know that...

35:12.821 --> 35:14.072
your line of work.

35:14.948 --> 35:16.157
And this looks like

35:16.157 --> 35:18.326
an unhinged, angry broad
got out of the loony bin

35:18.326 --> 35:20.412
and went on
a fuckin' killing spree.

35:20.954 --> 35:24.040
But, Councilman, look,
you got an opportunity here

35:24.040 --> 35:25.667
to give the people
someone to hate...

35:28.086 --> 35:29.045
and...

35:31.881 --> 35:33.091
someone to love.

35:35.552 --> 35:37.929
Sebastian Hady, that's the guy

35:38.054 --> 35:39.973
who turned the lights back on
in Crown Point...

35:42.058 --> 35:43.601
restored people's dignity,

35:44.227 --> 35:46.896
locked up the last Falcone,
ended a fuckin' drug war

35:46.896 --> 35:50.108
that's plagued
these city streets for decades.

35:50.859 --> 35:51.985
How does that sound?

35:53.028 --> 35:54.195
Sounds nice.

35:54.195 --> 35:56.948
Nice? [chuckles]
You fuckin' piece of shit.

35:58.241 --> 35:59.701
That's the kind of win
that you can ride

35:59.701 --> 36:01.536
all the way to the top,
Councilman.

36:06.249 --> 36:07.792
And in return?

36:08.293 --> 36:09.502
In return...

36:11.296 --> 36:12.130
Mmm.

36:12.797 --> 36:14.632
Might be good to feel welcome
in a place like this

36:14.758 --> 36:15.633
for a change.

36:16.634 --> 36:18.595
You know, meet some
of those friends you got.

36:19.471 --> 36:20.972
Hell, maybe, uh...

36:21.598 --> 36:23.725
one of these days,
we'll bump into Bella Reál.

36:24.476 --> 36:25.352
You know?

36:25.477 --> 36:27.228
[Hady chuckles]

36:27.228 --> 36:28.480
[ominous music playing]

36:35.695 --> 36:38.573
You're gonna have
some trouble, Oz.

36:39.282 --> 36:42.160
Reál, she's forming
a commission, anti-corruption.

36:42.702 --> 36:44.829
They're going after cops,
city officials.

36:44.954 --> 36:46.122
- Good.
- And they have a list

36:46.122 --> 36:48.166
of Carmine's associates.

36:48.291 --> 36:50.168
They're gonna subpoena you.

36:53.046 --> 36:54.172
You wanna be welcome?

36:55.131 --> 36:56.216
You gotta look...

36:58.176 --> 36:59.177
clean.

37:00.553 --> 37:02.055
As a fuckin' whistle...

37:03.598 --> 37:04.474
pal.

37:08.853 --> 37:09.896
[Hady chuckles]

37:15.527 --> 37:16.403
[door opens]

37:18.363 --> 37:19.531
[door closes]

37:19.656 --> 37:21.533
[music continues]

37:22.242 --> 37:23.743
[indistinct conversation]

37:25.662 --> 37:28.331
[man] Mayor-Elect, what can
you tell us on Crown Point?

37:28.331 --> 37:32.210
[Reál] Coordinating with GCPD.
All hospitals triaging.

37:32.335 --> 37:33.837
We're still searching
for survivors,

37:33.837 --> 37:35.588
but we need more resources.

37:35.588 --> 37:37.716
- Okay.
- [Reál] I'm relying on it.

37:37.841 --> 37:43.054
[conversation continues
indistinctly]

37:53.857 --> 37:54.899
[tense music playing]

38:12.625 --> 38:13.501
[music fades out]

38:21.801 --> 38:22.802
[Link] Oz.

38:24.429 --> 38:25.347
The fuck's this?

38:27.098 --> 38:29.184
[menacing music plays]

38:29.768 --> 38:30.852
Get in.

38:39.819 --> 38:41.780
[eerie, menacing music playing]

38:49.996 --> 38:52.123
[sentimental music plays]

38:55.168 --> 38:56.503
[phone vibrating]

39:05.637 --> 39:06.680
Mr. Zhao.

39:07.305 --> 39:08.223
[Zhao] I have Oz.

39:09.099 --> 39:11.393
[menacing music plays]

39:11.393 --> 39:13.103
- Fuckin' relax, Jesus!
- Come on.

39:13.103 --> 39:14.813
Should we bring him
to the house?

39:16.147 --> 39:17.315
Uh, I'm actually...

39:18.233 --> 39:20.110
packing up
the last of my things.

39:20.110 --> 39:22.862
Why don't I meet you
at Goodwin International?

39:22.862 --> 39:23.988
Hangar five.

39:24.489 --> 39:27.033
[breathes shakily]

39:27.158 --> 39:29.953
Congratulations, Mr. Zhao.

39:29.953 --> 39:31.413
[Zhao chuckles] And to you.

39:31.413 --> 39:33.039
[Sofia breathing shakily]

39:33.164 --> 39:36.167
["Where Did You Sleep Last
Night" by Sleigh Bells playing]

39:47.929 --> 39:49.639
[alcohol splashing]

39:50.306 --> 39:56.438
♪ My girl, my girl,
don't lie to me ♪

39:56.438 --> 40:01.526
♪ Tell me, where did you sleep
last night? ♪

40:02.944 --> 40:06.031
♪ In the pines, in the pines ♪

40:06.031 --> 40:09.200
♪ Where the sun
don't ever shine ♪

40:09.200 --> 40:13.705
♪ I would shiver
the whole night through ♪

40:18.251 --> 40:19.544
[fire whooshes]

40:19.669 --> 40:24.466
♪ My girl, my girl,
don't lie to me ♪

40:24.466 --> 40:28.887
♪ Tell me, where did you sleep
last night? ♪

40:29.971 --> 40:32.891
♪ In the pines, in the pines ♪

40:32.891 --> 40:35.560
♪ Where the sun
don't ever shine ♪

40:35.560 --> 40:39.898
♪ I would shiver
the whole night through ♪

40:41.107 --> 40:46.738
♪ My girl, my girl,
where will you go? ♪

40:46.863 --> 40:49.741
♪ I'm going
where the cold wind blows ♪

40:49.866 --> 40:51.076
[bottle shatters]

40:52.285 --> 40:54.913
♪ In the pines, in the pines ♪

40:55.038 --> 40:57.749
♪ Where the sun
don't ever shine ♪

40:57.874 --> 41:02.629
♪ I would shiver
the whole night through ♪

41:03.797 --> 41:10.095
[alcohol splashing]

41:11.304 --> 41:13.139
[bottle shatters]

41:15.600 --> 41:18.603
♪ In the pines, in the pines ♪

41:18.728 --> 41:21.773
♪ Where the sun
don't ever shine ♪

41:21.773 --> 41:26.611
♪ I would shiver
the whole night through ♪

41:28.029 --> 41:34.035
♪ My girl, my girl,
where will you go? ♪

41:34.035 --> 41:39.207
♪ I'm going
where the cold wind blows ♪

41:40.291 --> 41:43.253
♪ In the pines, in the pines ♪

41:43.378 --> 41:46.464
♪ Where the sun
don't ever shine ♪

41:46.464 --> 41:51.219
♪ I would shiver
the whole night through ♪

41:51.761 --> 41:52.929
[song ends]

41:52.929 --> 41:58.810
[glass shattering, explosions
inside house]

42:01.813 --> 42:02.647
[Enzo] Ma'am.

42:02.981 --> 42:04.983
[glass shattering,
explosions continue]

42:17.287 --> 42:18.663
[somber music playing]

42:22.500 --> 42:23.835
[engines revving]

42:31.051 --> 42:32.510
[somber music continues]

43:06.336 --> 43:08.254
[Oz breathing heavily]

43:08.755 --> 43:09.798
[car door closing]

43:14.844 --> 43:16.596
[aircraft flying overhead]

43:18.515 --> 43:19.891
[car door closes]

43:28.566 --> 43:30.985
Thank you, Mr. Zhao.

43:32.070 --> 43:33.613
Will you, uh, end things here

43:33.738 --> 43:35.699
or drop him over the Atlantic?

43:35.699 --> 43:37.200
See if the Penguin can fly?

43:37.200 --> 43:38.410
[laughs]

43:41.913 --> 43:43.581
[menacing music playing]

43:48.503 --> 43:49.963
Zhao...

43:49.963 --> 43:55.635
[guns firing]

43:55.760 --> 43:56.928
[bodyguard grunts]

43:57.554 --> 43:59.305
- [gun cocks]
- [Sofia panting]

43:59.431 --> 44:00.682
Hand it over.

44:02.267 --> 44:03.143
Slow.

44:12.068 --> 44:14.154
[Enzo moaning]

44:23.913 --> 44:25.832
What do ya say
you and me go for a drive?

44:27.500 --> 44:30.003
["O mio babbino caro" playing]

44:39.929 --> 44:41.348
Just like old times, huh?

44:45.185 --> 44:46.353
Were you goin' somewhere?

44:51.399 --> 44:52.984
I was hoping to.

45:01.451 --> 45:03.244
What did you say
to get Link to turn?

45:07.165 --> 45:08.249
I'm sure you...

45:09.668 --> 45:11.002
promised him something.

45:11.127 --> 45:13.838
Yeah, yeah. What you
and the Dai Lo never would.

45:15.340 --> 45:16.174
A shot.

45:17.342 --> 45:19.010
A chance to be somebody.

45:21.179 --> 45:23.014
Link was tired
of being overlooked.

45:23.848 --> 45:25.141
He ain't the only one neither.

45:25.141 --> 45:26.726
[grunting]

45:26.851 --> 45:28.937
[Oz] Years of being
brushed aside,

45:28.937 --> 45:32.232
laughed at, told to eat shit
and fuckin' like it.

45:32.357 --> 45:33.233
It breaks ya.

45:34.651 --> 45:35.860
Makes ya wanna break
somebody else.

45:35.985 --> 45:36.986
- [grunts]
- [grunts]

45:36.986 --> 45:37.987
[body thuds]

45:38.697 --> 45:40.073
[wet thudding]

45:40.198 --> 45:42.826
Figured you woulda
understood that, you know,

45:43.326 --> 45:44.202
considerin'...

45:45.495 --> 45:47.664
But you... you and your kind,

45:47.664 --> 45:50.375
you're so busy fillin'
your own fuckin' plate.

45:51.209 --> 45:53.378
You don't see that
everyone around you is starvin'.

45:54.087 --> 45:55.547
You got no idea
what it feels like,

45:55.672 --> 45:57.048
- born into nothin'.
- [gunshot]

45:57.173 --> 45:58.425
[Oz] Havin' to smile
at the person

45:58.425 --> 45:59.551
whose boot's on your neck.

45:59.676 --> 46:00.719
- [grunts]
- [sword slices]

46:00.969 --> 46:03.179
[Oz] Hopin' one day,
they'll look down,

46:03.179 --> 46:04.556
see ya there, and just let up.

46:04.681 --> 46:06.891
[wet gurgling]

46:07.017 --> 46:09.060
You know what people'll do
to push that down?

46:09.644 --> 46:11.271
They'll do fuckin' anything.

46:11.396 --> 46:13.273
Anything to push down
that feeling.

46:14.691 --> 46:16.067
You think
I don't understand that?

46:16.192 --> 46:17.444
[Oz scoffs]

46:18.862 --> 46:19.738
Right.

46:22.866 --> 46:25.326
[snorts] It doesn't matter.

46:27.579 --> 46:29.247
[chuckles wryly]

46:30.331 --> 46:32.000
Oswald Cobb...

46:33.793 --> 46:36.129
man of the people.

46:37.213 --> 46:38.256
That's right.

46:39.341 --> 46:41.301
That's what you need
to believe, huh?

46:45.221 --> 46:46.181
Here we are.

46:47.891 --> 46:49.434
["O mio babbino caro" ends]

47:26.680 --> 47:28.682
You don't wanna put your gun
to my back...

47:29.974 --> 47:31.309
make a big show of it?

47:31.434 --> 47:33.311
Nah. You ain't the type to run.

47:33.978 --> 47:35.063
[Sofia chuckles wryly]

47:44.197 --> 47:45.323
How's your mom?

47:46.866 --> 47:48.493
Has she told you
she loves you yet?

47:53.039 --> 47:53.915
Turn around.

47:55.834 --> 47:56.835
You were right.

47:58.628 --> 48:00.046
I didn't see you.

48:01.256 --> 48:02.257
But she did.

48:02.257 --> 48:04.009
She knew it
from the very beginning.

48:05.802 --> 48:07.721
You have always been a monster.

48:11.016 --> 48:13.476
You're never gonna find peace,
you know that?

48:13.977 --> 48:15.228
A sick fuck like you.

48:18.356 --> 48:19.524
You're going to hell...

48:20.692 --> 48:21.693
sweetheart.

48:24.696 --> 48:27.198
[tense music playing]

48:28.783 --> 48:30.118
I'll save you a seat.

48:37.042 --> 48:37.917
[gun cocks]

48:58.521 --> 48:59.397
[Sofia exhales]

49:01.566 --> 49:02.609
[music intensifies]

49:10.950 --> 49:13.578
- [helicopter blades whirring]
- [music fades]

49:16.289 --> 49:18.333
[sirens approaching]

49:21.461 --> 49:22.962
[dramatic music playing]

49:23.880 --> 49:25.465
[sirens blaring]

49:25.590 --> 49:26.925
[Bock] On the ground!

49:28.093 --> 49:30.011
Hands behind your back.

49:30.595 --> 49:31.471
Now!

49:38.895 --> 49:40.605
[handcuffs jangle]

49:42.524 --> 49:43.525
[Bock] Get her up.

49:52.617 --> 49:53.993
[dramatic music continues]

49:59.624 --> 50:01.543
There she is. You all right, Ma?

50:01.543 --> 50:03.962
- [indistinct newscast on TV]
- Get some cups.

50:04.087 --> 50:06.923
Snuck you in a little whiskey
to celebrate.

50:06.923 --> 50:07.966
Fuckin' did it, Ma.

50:08.091 --> 50:09.843
Fuckin' beautiful.

50:09.968 --> 50:11.511
This is what I'm talkin' about.
Look.

50:11.636 --> 50:13.179
...to the crooked politics

50:13.179 --> 50:15.515
that have allowed
wealthy elites

50:15.515 --> 50:17.475
like Sofia Falcone
to wreak havoc...

50:17.600 --> 50:18.393
[Oz] This is all me.

50:18.393 --> 50:19.561
...on the hardworking people...

50:19.561 --> 50:20.645
I fed him this bullshit.

50:20.770 --> 50:22.313
Look at him spittin' it out, Ma.

50:23.940 --> 50:24.899
What do you think?

50:26.526 --> 50:27.402
What do you...

50:28.987 --> 50:29.988
What do you think?

50:32.240 --> 50:33.116
Ma?

50:34.159 --> 50:36.494
Thank you, Councilman Hady,
for your...

50:36.619 --> 50:37.996
- Ma?
- ...continued service.

50:38.997 --> 50:39.914
Ma.

50:40.707 --> 50:41.708
Ma, look at me.

50:42.459 --> 50:43.585
Ma, look at me.

50:44.169 --> 50:45.003
Ma.

50:46.504 --> 50:47.380
Ma.

50:49.299 --> 50:51.176
- [Victor] Oz...
- Jesus fuck!

50:51.968 --> 50:54.888
Help-- Vic, she needs some help.
Get somebody in here.

50:55.013 --> 50:57.182
Get a doctor in here.
Get a doctor!

50:59.392 --> 51:00.435
Ma, Ma, Ma, look at me.

51:00.435 --> 51:02.187
[Victor] We need some help here.
Please!

51:02.687 --> 51:04.230
Hey, come here. Look at me, Ma.

51:04.230 --> 51:06.232
- [Victor] Hey, hey! Help!
- Look at me, sweetheart.

51:06.232 --> 51:08.985
- Ma. Come on.
- [nurse] Sir?

51:08.985 --> 51:10.904
There's somethin' wrong.
You gotta help.

51:10.904 --> 51:12.238
We've been looking for you

51:12.238 --> 51:13.531
but didn't know how
to reach you.

51:13.656 --> 51:14.908
Why aren't her eyes
fuckin' movin'?

51:14.908 --> 51:15.867
[nurse sighs]

51:16.409 --> 51:18.745
Your mother has suffered
a serious stroke.

51:23.500 --> 51:24.376
What?

51:25.377 --> 51:26.711
[nurse] I'm so sorry.

51:28.713 --> 51:30.298
What... what's goin' on?

51:31.758 --> 51:33.510
[nurse] I'm afraid
the stroke has left her

51:33.510 --> 51:35.804
in a persistent
vegetative state,

51:35.804 --> 51:38.598
and given your mother's age
and her Lewy body diagnosis--

51:38.598 --> 51:40.183
Whoa! What the fuck
you talkin' bout?

51:40.183 --> 51:43.937
[spluttering] You sayin'
she's a fuckin' vegetable?

51:45.021 --> 51:47.065
Her fuckin' eyes are open. Look!

51:47.190 --> 51:49.067
She's lookin'
at fuckin' somethin'.

51:49.192 --> 51:50.360
[nurse] I'm so sorry.

51:50.360 --> 51:51.903
Stop sayin'
you're fuckin' sorry!

51:52.028 --> 51:53.530
- Sir--
- You're another fuckin' idiot.

51:53.530 --> 51:54.948
Get the doctors in here!

51:55.240 --> 51:58.493
Get the fuckin' doctors in here!
Get a fuckin' doctor in here!

52:00.120 --> 52:01.621
[breathing heavily]

52:14.718 --> 52:16.761
[breathing shakily]

52:18.138 --> 52:19.014
[sniffs]

52:22.726 --> 52:23.852
Come on, doll.

52:25.145 --> 52:26.104
Look at me.

52:29.315 --> 52:30.275
I did it.

52:32.193 --> 52:35.155
I took it all
from those pricks...

52:38.074 --> 52:39.117
like you said.

52:43.079 --> 52:44.539
I'm the fucking king.

52:46.791 --> 52:48.710
[breathing heavily]

52:52.339 --> 52:53.381
Fuck, Ma.

52:54.299 --> 52:57.677
[breathing shakily]
Ma, don't do this to me.

53:00.930 --> 53:04.309
[sniffs] Ma, just don't do this
to me, all right?

53:06.144 --> 53:08.104
Ma, you can't do this to me,
please!

53:09.105 --> 53:11.816
[sniffs] You gotta tell me--
Just tell me you're proud of me.

53:12.859 --> 53:15.320
Ma, tell me
you're proud of me, please!

53:15.320 --> 53:17.530
Come on. Just once.
Just tell me you're proud of me.

53:17.530 --> 53:18.990
Tell me I did good!

53:20.158 --> 53:21.785
[sniffs] Tell me I did good!

53:23.495 --> 53:25.663
I did it for you, Ma!
I did it all for you,

53:25.789 --> 53:27.082
the whole thing!

53:27.082 --> 53:29.334
Your son, I'm the fucking king!

53:29.459 --> 53:30.835
It's what you wanted, Ma.

53:31.294 --> 53:33.171
[crying] It's what you wanted.

53:34.839 --> 53:37.842
Ma, please, just once...
Just once...

53:37.967 --> 53:42.681
[sobbing]

53:42.806 --> 53:43.890
[tender music playing]

53:47.185 --> 53:49.729
[sobbing continues]

54:00.490 --> 54:01.366
[music fades out]

54:05.870 --> 54:07.205
Don't feel like it should.

54:09.874 --> 54:10.959
No.

54:10.959 --> 54:12.961
Don't know what happened.
She was fine.

54:16.339 --> 54:17.716
[swallows, sighs]

54:18.383 --> 54:19.384
[chuckles]

54:21.553 --> 54:23.388
Everything I ever done
was for her.

54:27.267 --> 54:28.643
But in the end...

54:31.438 --> 54:32.397
I don't know.

54:35.066 --> 54:36.776
Sh-she knew that.

54:39.070 --> 54:40.071
She did.

54:42.949 --> 54:44.576
You think she forgives me?

54:45.785 --> 54:46.828
For what?

54:53.376 --> 54:54.419
I don't know.

54:55.587 --> 54:56.755
All kinds of things.

54:59.049 --> 55:00.925
None of this came easy,
you know.

55:04.054 --> 55:05.680
Can't stop thinkin' about 'em.

55:08.558 --> 55:10.143
My brothers.
What kinda men they'd be

55:10.268 --> 55:11.478
if they had the chance.

55:14.022 --> 55:15.273
What they'd think of me...

55:17.442 --> 55:18.485
now.

55:20.236 --> 55:21.654
Yeah, I th...

55:22.405 --> 55:23.615
I think about that too.

55:24.699 --> 55:26.201
My family...

55:28.411 --> 55:29.454
I miss 'em.

55:32.415 --> 55:34.834
Yeah, I r-- I really miss 'em.

55:35.919 --> 55:37.128
Yeah.

55:41.466 --> 55:43.134
Here, take the rest.

55:49.641 --> 55:50.642
[Victor exhales sharply]

55:53.311 --> 55:55.855
You know I couldn't've done any
of this shit without ya, right?

55:57.107 --> 55:58.108
You know that?

55:59.234 --> 56:01.903
Bringin' Link into the fold,
I didn't see it at first, but...

56:03.321 --> 56:04.656
it was a smart move.

56:08.326 --> 56:09.661
You did good, kid.

56:12.080 --> 56:12.956
Thanks.

56:15.166 --> 56:16.209
[chuckles]

56:19.337 --> 56:20.880
And thanks for, uh...

56:22.841 --> 56:24.718
Thanks for taking a chance
on me.

56:26.344 --> 56:27.345
F-f...

56:28.388 --> 56:30.181
For taking me in.

56:33.810 --> 56:35.020
You're like...

56:35.979 --> 56:37.063
You're f...

56:38.356 --> 56:39.607
You're f...

56:40.191 --> 56:41.568
f-family to me.

56:42.235 --> 56:43.194
You know?

56:43.319 --> 56:45.113
[somber music playing]

56:52.829 --> 56:53.913
Fuck.

56:55.081 --> 56:56.041
[sniffs]

56:59.878 --> 57:01.212
Fuck, Vic.

57:02.172 --> 57:03.214
You and me...

57:04.924 --> 57:06.384
it's all that's left.

57:11.139 --> 57:13.391
Now, I don't believe
in kismet or nothin'.

57:15.185 --> 57:16.394
[Victor] Hmm.

57:17.354 --> 57:18.813
But... [sighs]

57:19.606 --> 57:20.815
It's good that we met.

57:21.399 --> 57:22.817
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

57:23.651 --> 57:26.404
You've seen me at my lowest,
all this shit with my ma.

57:28.198 --> 57:29.324
You've been there...

57:31.743 --> 57:33.745
by my side, every fuckin' step.

57:36.664 --> 57:37.957
But listen, kid.

57:40.585 --> 57:41.753
I, uh...

57:44.381 --> 57:46.257
I can't bring you with me
this time.

57:48.510 --> 57:49.594
What do you mean?

57:50.428 --> 57:52.472
I mean, that's the thing
about family.

57:53.098 --> 57:54.849
- Oz...
- [music turns tense]

57:54.849 --> 57:56.935
- It's your strength.
- Oz, what are you--

57:57.060 --> 57:58.311
- It drives you.
- [choking]

57:58.937 --> 58:00.939
But fuck if it don't
make ya weak, too.

58:01.064 --> 58:02.482
Oz! Oz!

58:03.149 --> 58:04.818
And I can't have that no more.

58:04.818 --> 58:06.319
Oz... [gasps]

58:07.570 --> 58:08.363
Please... Please...

58:08.363 --> 58:09.823
I can't have that shit. I can't.

58:09.948 --> 58:11.533
Please... Please... [gasping]

58:11.533 --> 58:13.952
Oz... Oz... Oz...

58:14.077 --> 58:16.037
- It's too much.
- Please...

58:16.830 --> 58:18.623
- Too fuckin' much.
- [choking] Oz...

58:18.748 --> 58:20.709
[choking]

58:20.709 --> 58:21.960
I'm sorry.

58:22.085 --> 58:25.964
[choking]

58:27.799 --> 58:30.468
I'm sorry.
You're a good man, Vic.

58:31.302 --> 58:32.429
You got a good heart.

58:32.429 --> 58:37.142
[choking]

58:37.267 --> 58:38.309
[gasping]

58:38.435 --> 58:39.936
[Oz breathing heavily]

58:39.936 --> 58:41.604
[choking, gasping stop]

58:44.482 --> 58:45.900
It wasn't for nothin'.

58:50.655 --> 58:53.491
[breathing heavily]

59:10.342 --> 59:12.010
[grunting]

59:48.046 --> 59:49.089
[water splashes]

59:52.509 --> 59:53.551
[water lapping]

59:59.182 --> 01:00:02.394
- [rumbling]
- [people clamoring]

01:00:02.519 --> 01:00:03.478
[door slams]

01:00:03.478 --> 01:00:05.563
[patients shouting in distance]

01:00:05.689 --> 01:00:06.648
[buzzer sounds]

01:00:13.905 --> 01:00:15.949
- [door thuds, locks]
- [buzzer sounds]

01:00:17.909 --> 01:00:19.077
[eerie music playing]

01:00:23.248 --> 01:00:24.833
[Julian, muffled]
I brought your mail.

01:00:33.216 --> 01:00:34.592
Mostly the usual.

01:00:36.052 --> 01:00:37.345
Rants, poems,

01:00:38.096 --> 01:00:39.264
marriage proposals.

01:00:43.518 --> 01:00:44.686
This one's different.

01:00:46.396 --> 01:00:47.605
I think you should read it.

01:00:50.567 --> 01:00:52.652
It's from a woman
named Selina Kyle.

01:00:55.947 --> 01:00:57.782
She says she's your half-sister.

01:00:57.907 --> 01:00:58.742
[paper rustles]

01:00:58.742 --> 01:00:59.868
[eerie music ends]

01:01:03.246 --> 01:01:04.122
[Julian] Sofia?

01:01:07.000 --> 01:01:08.668
[shouting in distance]

01:01:14.591 --> 01:01:16.009
- [buzzer sounds]
- [door unlocks]

01:01:20.513 --> 01:01:22.515
- [door closes, locks]
- [buzzer sounds]

01:01:34.486 --> 01:01:35.653
[gentle music playing]

01:01:39.074 --> 01:01:44.579
[breathing heavily]

01:01:53.505 --> 01:01:54.506
[chuckles softly]

01:01:55.507 --> 01:01:56.549
[sirens in distance]

01:01:58.510 --> 01:01:59.344
[car alarm beeps]

01:02:12.107 --> 01:02:13.108
[elevator dings]

01:02:43.346 --> 01:02:44.889
[medical equipment beeping]

01:02:51.938 --> 01:02:53.148
[Oz sighs]

01:02:55.275 --> 01:02:56.651
How we doin' today?

01:02:58.236 --> 01:02:59.571
You feelin' any better?

01:03:00.196 --> 01:03:01.448
You look better.

01:03:17.881 --> 01:03:19.132
I know.

01:03:21.593 --> 01:03:22.844
It's everything you wanted.

01:03:31.102 --> 01:03:34.314
["If This Is Goodbye"
by Margaret Whiting playing]

01:03:34.439 --> 01:03:36.649
[chuckles]

01:03:41.571 --> 01:03:45.533
♪ I may walk in sunlight ♪

01:03:45.533 --> 01:03:51.623
♪ So golden
it is glory to behold... ♪

01:03:51.748 --> 01:03:52.874
There she is.

01:03:54.292 --> 01:03:55.460
[Eve] Oswald.

01:03:56.294 --> 01:04:01.800
♪ Only shadows I'll see ♪

01:04:01.925 --> 01:04:03.009
You look beautiful.

01:04:04.636 --> 01:04:06.221
Dance with me, sweetheart.

01:04:08.682 --> 01:04:12.560
♪ I may hear sweet music ♪

01:04:12.560 --> 01:04:19.442
♪ Whose tones
and glowing harmonies abound ♪

01:04:19.442 --> 01:04:26.074
♪ But all their silver sound
will be discord ♪

01:04:26.074 --> 01:04:27.617
♪ To me... ♪

01:04:27.617 --> 01:04:29.160
Tell me you love me.

01:04:30.453 --> 01:04:32.497
I love you, Oswald.

01:04:35.792 --> 01:04:37.210
Tell me you're proud of me.

01:04:37.794 --> 01:04:40.922
I'm so proud of you.

01:04:40.922 --> 01:04:42.257
I did it, Ma.

01:04:43.550 --> 01:04:44.509
Didn't I?

01:04:46.094 --> 01:04:47.095
Tell me I did it.

01:04:47.095 --> 01:04:49.097
You did it. Mm-hmm.

01:04:49.097 --> 01:04:51.683
Top floor, penthouse.

01:04:52.475 --> 01:04:54.352
No one above ya or beside ya.

01:04:54.978 --> 01:04:56.521
I knew you would.

01:04:57.731 --> 01:04:59.691
My beautiful boy.

01:04:59.816 --> 01:05:04.070
♪ ...to say to me
the things I need to know ♪

01:05:04.070 --> 01:05:06.031
Gotham's yours, sweetheart.

01:05:08.825 --> 01:05:10.952
Nothin' is standin'
in your way now.

01:05:11.995 --> 01:05:13.288
God damn right.

01:05:15.331 --> 01:05:20.003
♪ Then love is a lie ♪

01:05:20.128 --> 01:05:27.093
♪ If this is goodbye ♪

01:05:31.556 --> 01:05:32.891
[music crescendos, ends]

01:05:34.934 --> 01:05:36.811
[tense music playing]

01:07:00.979 --> 01:07:02.022
[tense music continues]

01:07:51.029 --> 01:07:51.946
[music ends]
